stave 1

// Three Japanese joints, written to prove that joint kinds are pluggable:
// nothing here needs code in Stave itself.
//
//   ari_tsugi     simple: one cut per beam, one assembly step
//   kanawa_tsugi  complex: marked-out outlines, a key the joint makes, two steps
//   chidori       complex: three parts in one node and a quarter turn to lock
//
// These are samples for the format. Check a joinery reference (and make a
// trial piece) before cutting good timber from them.

library "Japanese joinery samples"
